-# Texture cache collector: at most this many microseconds per frame (unset: unlimited, Eden's
-# behaviour). It stops once the time is spent and goes on from the oldest image next frame; a
-# collection begun at the expected threshold keeps going down to a band under it before it rests;
-# and an image the GPU wrote (downloaded first, behind a full GPU wait) is evicted at most once
-# every 30 frames unless an allocation failed. Ocarina of Time on the Steam Deck spent 10-12 ms
-# of every frame (peaks of 37-72 ms) in the collector, on the GPU thread inside the present
-# (EDEN_DKB_FRAME_TRACE=1: "DKB tick ... texture_cache_ms=sum/max tc_gc_deletes= tc_gc_downloads=").
+# Texture cache collector under its critical threshold: at most this many microseconds per frame
+# (unset: unlimited, Eden's behaviour), after at least 2 deletions. It stops once the time is
+# spent and goes on from the oldest image next frame; a collection begun at the expected
+# threshold keeps going down to a band under it before it rests; and an image the GPU wrote
+# (downloaded first, behind a full GPU wait) is evicted at most once every 30 frames. At or past
+# critical, or when an image did not fit, the collector runs unbounded as before until the use is
+# back under: textures first, GPU-written images only if that was not enough. Ocarina of Time on
+# the Steam Deck spent 10-12 ms of every frame (peaks of 37-72 ms) in the collector, on the GPU
+# thread inside the present; with the budget applied past critical too, it stopped evicting and
+# the process grew until earlyoom killed it. EDEN_DKB_FRAME_TRACE=1 prints per second:
+# "DKB tick ... texture_cache_ms=sum/max tc_gc_deletes= tc_gc_downloads= tc_gc_examined=
+# tc_gc_critical_frames= tc_gc_budget_stops= tc_used_mib= tc_image_mib=".
 #EDEN_NX2_TC_GC_BUDGET_US=1000
 
 # =0: the collector counts its own images instead of reading the driver's device memory usage,
